SEC. 51P-153.108.YARD, LOT, AND SPACE REGULATIONS. (Note: The yard, lot, and space regulations in this section must be read together with the yard, lot, and space regulations in Division 51A-4.400. If there is a conflict between this section and Division 51A-4.400, this section controls.)
(a)In general.
(1)Except as provided in this section, the yard, lot, and space regulations for the GO(A) General Office District apply.
(2)Except as provided in this section, maximum structure height is 85 feet.
(b)Special project.
(1)Front yard. Except in areas shown on the development plan, minimum front yard is 15 feet measured from the Property line.
(A)Urban form setback. Urban form setback does not apply, but a setback of 25 feet is required for any portion of a building above 80 feet.
(B)Encroachments. The following may encroach into the front yard setback:
(i)architectural elements;
(ii)benches;
(iii)stoops;
(iv)patios;
(v)garage ventilation shafts;
(vi)raised planters;
(vii)seat walls and retaining walls;
(viii)stairs, and railings;
(xi)structures that are not fully enclosed such as canopies, colonnades that support building overhangs, and pergolas;
(x)city required utilities; and
(xi)ordinary projections of window sills, bay windows, belt courses, cornices, eaves, art, fountains, balconies, and other architectural features.
(2)Side and rear yard.
(A)Except as provided in this Paragraph, minimum side and rear yard is 20 feet measured from the Property line.
(B)For any portion of structure 80 feet or taller, minimum side and rear yard is 25 feet.
(C)Tower spacing does not apply.
(3)Floor area ratio. If compliant with Section 51P-153.113, 51P-153.114, and 51P-153.115, the maximum floor area ratio is 7.0.
(4)Height. If compliant with Sections 51P-153.113, 51P-153.114, and 51P-153.115, maximum structure height is 285 feet. Ordinary projections listed in Section 51A-4.408 and wind turbines may exceed the maximum height by 12 feet.
(5)Lot coverage. Maximum lot coverage is 80 percent. Aboveground parking structures are included in lot coverage calculations; surface parking lots and underground parking structures are not.
(6)Stories. No maximum number of stories.
(7)Micro units. A minimum of five percent of all residential units must be micro units. Micro units may not be used to fulfill the requirements of Section 51P-153-113. (Ord. Nos. 24729; 25508; 33227)
